ext("C061", " Report 65 (Rabit): 'Rabit's free tier was not a cost — it was the acquisition engine and the review engine' (48 reviews at 4.88); 'no ridiculous paywalls. everything you need is free'.")
ext("C133", " Report 65 (Rabit): §2.4 — 'Rabit monetises the number of habits. Its behavioural engine — plants, streaks, reminders — is what people love, and it rewards consistency, not volume. So the paywall taxes the axis users do not value while leaving the axis they do value free-but-broken'; a reviewer asks for exactly the inverse ('manter uma versão free com outras funcionalidades pagas mas não bloquear o uso do aplicativo'); M1: raise the cap materially and paywall depth instead of count; the paid tier 'não há grandes diferenças quando paga'.")
ext("C240", " Report 65 (Rabit): an interstitial on habit completion from 23 Dec 2022 — 'Cada que completo un hábito me aparece un anuncio!!!'; 'vengo a desinstalarla después de ver unos 40 anuncios'; 'They don't even let you finish what you were doing' — ADS_BAD 15 (3.01%, mean 2.33), 12 of 46 reviews in the launch window (26.1%); 'An app whose entire behavioural model is complete the habit → see your plant grow → feel rewarded inserted an interstitial exactly at the reward moment'; the close button rendered under the iPhone 13 status bar and forced a restart; F5.")
ext("C246", " Report 65 (Rabit): ads introduced into a formerly ad-free app cost it its distinguishing praise; a reviewer names the perceived intent — 'se o objetivo é fazer pagar o premium ou desistir de usar o app'; M5: consider removing ads for free users entirely and monetising on depth.")
